{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiFMAM1vtNAfzQswFmBP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (197 words, counted with `wc -w`). On the evidence set, PIN messages now mostly go to cards, and nothing else in the evidence changed route. All numbers below come from forward passes in `final.py`.\n\n**→ Evidence.** **16/32 → 27/32** correct. All 11 gains are PIN rows. The 16 non-PIN rows route exactly as before.\n\n**→ What changed.** I reused four hidden units that had almost no effect on the output (740, 771, 828, 1006). No other weights changed, and I added no extra module. Two of the units raise the cards score for PIN messages, and two lower the account_security score.\n\n**→ How the weights were set.** Each unit looks for \"this message is about a PIN\" as a difference of averages over 636 messages I wrote myself. I first removed the few dominant directions in the vectors, which mostly measure how well a message fits any department. Each unit gives a fixed push of up to 4 points, so it cannot swing too far. I used no training, solver or fitting to the evidence labels.\n\n**→ Earlier correction still holds.** All 11 exchange-rate messages I tested route exactly as before.\n\n**→ Risk.**\n- On PIN messages the edit had never seen, only **46 of 67** went to cards. Phrases like \"Changing my PIN\" and \"change pin at ATMs\" still go to account_security, as do 5 evidence rows.\n- **7 of 129** of my non-PIN test messages changed route, mostly age questions (\"Do I need to be 18?\"). I deliberately wrote that set to look like PIN messages, so on real messages the rate is probably lower. I can't confirm that without the hidden test set.\n\n**Also found:** the starting model already sends some complaints about a bad rate on a cash withdrawal to disputes, which goes against the first correction. My edit does not change that.\n\nMistake: I first built a capped push from low-gain GELU units, and they leaked small changes onto every message (about 40 extra route changes). Guard: every unit now uses a gain of 20. `final.py` fails if any weight outside the four units changes, and it prints how much logits move on non-PIN messages (median 0.0001). This project has no lessons file. If you want the guard recorded, `.work/review/MISSES.md` would be the place.\n\nFiles are in `step2/`:\n- scorer_out.npz\n- NOTES.md"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1405,"cache_read_input_tokens":200959,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1405},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"268d78b1-b622-4872-9e71-b1996eae119e","uuid":"8e78e243-d3d0-4e42-989a-97cdbd65f533","timestamp":"2026-11-04T17:02:32.329Z","request_id":"req_011CgiFMA68YbSkCCC28b2rS"}
